# This repo stores and checks out LF everywhere.
#
# Without a rule, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) writes CRLF into the
# working tree while the tools that generate files -- Go, npm, Vite -- write LF.
# A file can then end up with mixed endings, and appending to one produces a
# whole-file diff. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working tree matching the LF blobs
# git already stores.
#
# It also keeps gofmt honest: it reads a CRLF .go file as wholly misformatted
# and flags every Go source in the repo (see TECHNICAL_DEBTS.md D7).
#
# text=auto still lets git detect binary files and leave them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
